{#- History the user marked a character present as not knowing, so nobody
    on stage has any of it (spec 11, the `withheld` state). The narrator may
    keep continuity with it; the heading is secret lore's own instruction, so
    no character acts on it unless it reaches them on the page. Never in an
    NPC's prompt, under any name.
    Vars: history_blocks ([str]) or history_withheld ([EvidenceItem]). -#}
{%- from "scene/_secrecy.j2" import secret_block -%}
{%- set blocks = history_blocks if history_blocks is defined else [] -%}
{%- if history_blocks is not defined -%}
{%- for item in history_withheld -%}
{%- set block -%}{%- include "scene/sections/history_item.j2" -%}{%- endset -%}
{%- set _ = blocks.append(block.strip()) -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if blocks %}# Earlier in the campaign, kept from the cast

{{ secret_block(blocks) }}{% endif -%}
